---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="values - based.health">
    <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Values & Principles</h2>
        <p class="py-2">
            based.health is built on a few simple rules. Since this is a
            community project, these values help us decide what protocols and
            products belong here and what should be rejected.
        </p>
    </div>

    <main class="py-8 space-y-10">
        <section>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-[#a64d79] uppercase text-sm mb-2">
                1. Safety Before Optimization
            </h3>
            <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Health advice has downside risk. Protocols should be boring,
                low-risk, and explicit about who should modify or avoid them.
                The starter kit does not include medical treatment, extreme
                interventions, or anything that needs professional supervision.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-[#a64d79] uppercase text-sm mb-2">
                2. The Community is the Boss
            </h3>
            <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed">
                There is no company behind this. It is a public directory. If
                you see a product that is actually unhealthy or a protocol that
                is wrong, you are encouraged to fix it via GitHub.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-[#a64d79] uppercase text-sm mb-2">
                3. Zero Marketing Noise
            </h3>
            <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed">
                We don't do ads, sponsorships, affiliate placement, or
                influencer laundering. If something is listed, it should be
                useful without needing a sales pitch.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-[#a64d79] uppercase text-sm mb-2">
                4. Stupid Simple
            </h3>
            <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Health should be easy to understand. We keep the language plain
                and the steps clear so someone can implement the protocol before
                reading deeper context.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-[#a64d79] uppercase text-sm mb-2">
                5. Evidence Has Grades
            </h3>
            <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Not every useful practice has the same proof. Protocols should
                show whether support is strong, moderate, or emerging, and the
                claim should be no stronger than the evidence.
            </p>
        </section>
    </main>
</BaseLayout>
